B.Fu=s(["Layer 2, single hop. Switches do not forward LLDP or CDP frames. You only ever see the device on the other end of your own cable, never anything past it.","Wired only. These frames do not cross Wi-Fi. A laptop on Wi-Fi sees nothing; you must be on the wired NIC (on a Mac, usually a USB or Thunderbolt Ethernet adapter).","The switch has to have it turned on. Cisco IOS runs CDP by default but ships LLDP off; many non-Cisco switches also ship LLDP off. When nothing shows up, first check whether the switch is sending, not whether your tool is broken."],t.s)
